WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.343 --> 00:00:02.519
(cheerful accordion music)

00:00:02.519 --> 00:00:06.186
(speaking foreign language)

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.250
- [Narrator] In the middle
of the French Pyrenees,

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.760
there's a cake that's been spinning

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:24.210
and spinning and spinning
for over two centuries.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.950
Joseph here has formed a society

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.483
to keep the recipe going.

00:00:28.844 --> 00:00:32.511
(speaking foreign language)

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.470
- [Narrator] And he's in charge of a cake

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:37.495
with quite a curious past.

00:00:37.495 --> 00:00:41.162
(speaking foreign language)

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.200
- [Narrator] The cake is
a reminder that losing

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.830
isn't always bad.

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:53.460
As Napoleon's soldiers
retreated from Russia,

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.480
they picked up the recipe

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.487
from several Eastern European countries,

00:00:56.487 --> 00:00:59.270
and brought it all the
way to the Pyrenees,

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:02.080
where many people, including
Joseph and his brotherhood,

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.841
have kept the baking going.

00:01:03.841 --> 00:01:07.508
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:14.617 --> 00:01:15.804
- [Narrator] So, what's in it?

00:01:15.804 --> 00:01:19.471
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.249
- [Narrator] Doesn't that hurt your arm?

00:01:50.249 --> 00:01:53.916
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:57.403 --> 00:02:00.236
(whimsical music)

00:02:35.648 --> 00:02:38.398
(resonant tone)

